---
// Home page hero — security/compliance remediation positioning for the
// London market. Single column, buyer-facing headline; the platform.tf
// code window moved to /approach so the first screen speaks to the
// audit-owner, not the engineer. Teal and silver glows retained.
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <!-- Background glows — pure CSS radial gradients, no assets.
       pointer-events-none so they never intercept clicks. -->
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true">
    <div
      class="absolute -top-32 right-[-10%] h-[34rem] w-[34rem]"
      style="background: radial-gradient(circle, rgb(0 161 155 / 0.14) 0%, rgb(0 161 155 / 0.05) 40%, transparent 70%)"
    ></div>
    <div
      class="absolute -left-40 top-24 h-[28rem] w-[28rem]"
      style="background: radial-gradient(circle, rgb(200 204 206 / 0.07) 0%, transparent 65%)"
    ></div>
  </div>

  <div class="container-page relative py-20 md:py-28 lg:py-32">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-6">Azure security &amp; compliance</p>

      <h1 class="hero-gradient mb-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight leading-[1.08] text-balance md:text-5xl">
        Azure security and compliance remediation for London-market insurers.
      </h1>

      <p class="body-muted max-w-2xl text-lg">
        Audit findings fixed in code, with evidence &mdash; Entra&nbsp;ID,
        PIM, Conditional Access, Key&nbsp;Vault, Defender for Cloud, and
        Terraform. For Lloyd&rsquo;s market insurers and regulated
        financial services firms. CAF and Well-Architected aligned
        throughout.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="mailto:alex@harvtech.co.uk" class="btn-primary text-base">
          Talk to us
        </a>
        <a href="/services/security-hardening" class="btn-secondary text-base">
          How remediation works
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
